    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137093",
      "type": "stage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "scenedesc"
      ],
      "text": "Alarum. Excursions. Enter Falstaff and Colevile, meeting.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [
        {
          "tag": "span",
          "start": 26,
          "end": 34,
          "className": "charname"
        },
        {
          "tag": "span",
          "start": 39,
          "end": 47,
          "className": "charname"
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137093/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 57,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1834800,
        "end": 1834943,
        "line": 68688,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@137093",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": null,
      "attribution": {
        "status": "not-applicable"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137240",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FALSTAFF.\nWhat’s your name, sir? Of what condition are you, and of what place, I pray?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137240/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137240/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 86,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1834947,
        "end": 1835064,
        "line": 68691,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@137240",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FALSTAFF.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137361",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "COLEVILE.\nI am a knight, sir, and my name is Colevile of the Dale.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137361/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137361/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 66,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1835068,
        "end": 1835164,
        "line": 68697,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@137361",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "COLEVILE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137461",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FALSTAFF.\nWell, then, Colevile is your name, a knight is your degree, and your place the Dale. Colevile shall be still your name, a traitor your degree, and the dungeon your place, a place deep enough; so shall you be still Colevile of the Dale.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137461/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137461/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 245,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1835168,
        "end": 1835445,
        "line": 68702,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@137461",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FALSTAFF.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137742",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "COLEVILE.\nAre not you Sir John Falstaff?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137742/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137742/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 40,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1835449,
        "end": 1835519,
        "line": 68709,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@137742",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "COLEVILE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137816",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FALSTAFF.\nAs good a man as he, sir, whoe’er I am. Do ye yield, sir, or shall I sweat for you? If I do sweat, they are the drops of thy lovers, and they weep for thy death. Therefore rouse up fear and trembling, and do observance to my mercy.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137816/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@137816/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 241,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1835523,
        "end": 1835797,
        "line": 68714,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@137816",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FALSTAFF.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138094",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "COLEVILE.\nI think you are Sir John Falstaff, and in that thought yield me.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138094/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138094/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 74,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1835801,
        "end": 1835905,
        "line": 68722,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@138094",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "COLEVILE.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138202",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FALSTAFF.\nI have a whole school of tongues in this belly of mine, and not a tongue of them all speaks any other word but my name. An I had but a belly of any indifferency, I were simply the most active fellow in Europe. My womb, my womb, my womb undoes me. Here comes our general.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138202/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138202/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 280,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1835909,
        "end": 1836222,
        "line": 68727,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@138202",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FALSTAFF.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138519",
      "type": "stage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "scenedesc"
      ],
      "text": "Enter Prince John of Lancaster, Westmoreland, Blunt, and others.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [
        {
          "tag": "span",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 51,
          "className": "charname"
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138519/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 64,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1836226,
        "end": 1836346,
        "line": 68735,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@138519",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": null,
      "attribution": {
        "status": "not-applicable"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138643",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "LANCASTER.\nThe heat is past; follow no further now.\nCall in the powers, good cousin Westmoreland.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138643/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138643/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 51,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138643/line-3",
          "start": 52,
          "end": 97,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1836350,
        "end": 1836482,
        "line": 68738,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@138643",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "LANCASTER.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138779",
      "type": "passage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "right"
      ],
      "text": "[Exit Westmoreland.]",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [
        {
          "tag": "span",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 18,
          "className": "charname"
        },
        {
          "tag": "i",
          "start": 1,
          "end": 19
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138779/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 20,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1836486,
        "end": 1836565,
        "line": 68744,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@138779",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": null,
      "attribution": {
        "status": "source-unlabelled"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138862",
      "type": "passage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "Now, Falstaff, where have you been all this while?\nWhen everything is ended, then you come.\nThese tardy tricks of yours will, on my life,\nOne time or other break some gallows’ back.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138862/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 50,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138862/line-2",
          "start": 51,
          "end": 91,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138862/line-3",
          "start": 92,
          "end": 137,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@138862/line-4",
          "start": 138,
          "end": 181,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1836569,
        "end": 1836790,
        "line": 68746,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@138862",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": null,
      "attribution": {
        "status": "source-unlabelled"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139087",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FALSTAFF.\nI would be sorry, my lord, but it should be thus. I never knew yet but rebuke and check was the reward of valour. Do you think me a swallow, an arrow, or a bullet? Have I, in my poor and old motion, the expedition of thought? I have speeded hither with the very extremest inch of possibility; I have foundered nine score and odd posts; and here, travel-tainted as I am, have in my pure and immaculate valour, taken Sir John Colevile of the Dale, a most furious knight and valorous enemy. But what of that? He saw me, and yielded; that I may justly say, with the hook-nosed fellow of Rome, “I came, saw, and overcame.”",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139087/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139087/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 627,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1836794,
        "end": 1837459,
        "line": 68753,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@139087",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FALSTAFF.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139756",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "LANCASTER.\nIt was more of his courtesy than your deserving.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139756/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139756/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 59,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1837463,
        "end": 1837552,
        "line": 68766,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@139756",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "LANCASTER.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139849",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FALSTAFF.\nI know not. Here he is, and here I yield him. And I beseech your Grace, let it be booked with the rest of this day’s deeds, or, by the Lord, I will have it in a particular ballad else, with mine own picture on the top on’t, Colevile kissing my foot: to the which course if I be enforced, if you do not all show like gilt twopences to me, and I in the clear sky of fame o’ershine you as much as the full moon doth the cinders of the element, which show like pins’ heads to her, believe not the word of the noble. Therefore let me have right, and let desert mount.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139849/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@139849/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 572,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1837556,
        "end": 1838165,
        "line": 68771,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@139849",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FALSTAFF.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@140462",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "LANCASTER.\nThine’s too heavy to mount.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@140462/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@140462/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 38,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1838169,
        "end": 1838237,
        "line": 68783,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@140462",
        "anchor": "sceneIV_10.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "LANCASTER.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@140534",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FALSTAFF.\nLet it shine, then.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneIV_10.3/p@140534/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
